{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And he called it El, the Elohim of Israel.</b> In his prayer he called the blessed El 'Elohim,' as seen in his saying וְהָיָה ה' לִי לֵאלֹהִים (Genesis 28:21) — and this when he is Israel, so that the nations of the world cannot make him turn aside from his own resolve and from the resolve of his Maker, as he mentioned in his vow above (Genesis 28:20–22)."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:33:10.208215323Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}